Package: form.validation
Title: Validate Submitted Data Against Neutral Form Models
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R:
    person("Tony", "Chemit", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "dev@tchemit.fr")
Description: Generates and executes structural and field checks from explicit
    form models. Validates supplied worksheet data and reference values,
    supports custom rules, and returns findings with source coordinates and
    execution status. Provides an Excel input adapter and exports
    single-input CSV and HTML reports. The engine accepts supplied data without
    workbook readers or databases.
License: LGPL-2.1
URL: https://ultreia-io.github.io/form.validation/,
    https://github.com/ultreia-io/form.validation
BugReports: https://github.com/ultreia-io/form.validation/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: cellranger, digest, jsonlite, form.model (>= 0.5.1), parallel, readxl,
    tools, yaml (>= 2.3.10)
Suggests: form.references (== 0.1.0), knitr, openxlsx,
    rmarkdown, testthat (>= 3.0.0), xml2
Remotes: ultreia-io/form.model@v0.5.1,
    ultreia-io/form.references@v0.1.0
VignetteBuilder: knitr
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/Needs/coverage: covr, xml2
Config/Needs/website: pkgdown, covr, htmltools, xml2
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.1
